# Reviewed exceptions for the OnePromptMan leak scanner (function-core build/leak_scan.py).
# One regex per line, matched against the flagged text only: HIT, or PATH :: HIT.

# The project's own name. It is here because this public repo's own name matches a
# private-layer rule (meant for other repos), and the private layer cannot pass without
# it. The maintainer decides whether this exception moves to the private rules' allow list.
^chimera$

# Test fixtures, not real data: a placeholder git identity, a generic home path inside
# recorded test output, and a deliberately odd fake operator token.
^tests/conftest\.py$ :: ^test@chimera\.local$
^tests/data/verification-20260904-tick-stamp-durability\.json$ :: ^/home/user$
^tests/test_g2_token\.py$ :: ^token = "-not-a-flag-just-unlucky$
